## Setup
Let $m := 0.5\,\mathrm{kg}$, $k := 20\,\mathrm{N/m}$, $c := 0.4\,\mathrm{N\,s/m}$ and $x_0 := 0.1\,\mathrm m$.

$$ m\ddot x + c\dot x + kx = 0, \quad x(0) = x_0, \ \dot x(0) = 0 $$

## Results
$$ \omega_0 := \sqrt{\frac{k}{m}} \approx ? \qquad \zeta := \frac{c}{2\sqrt{km}} \approx ? \qquad \omega_d := \omega_0\sqrt{1 - \zeta^2} \approx ? $$
$$ T_d := \frac{2\pi}{\omega_d} \approx ? \qquad \delta := \frac{2\pi\zeta}{\sqrt{1 - \zeta^2}} \approx ? $$

$$ E(t) := \tfrac12 m \dot x^2 + \tfrac12 k x^2 $$
$$ \frac{dE}{dt} \le 0 \ \text{ for all } t \ge 0 \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

Figure: $x(t)$ and the envelope $\pm x_0 e^{-\zeta\omega_0 t}$, $t \in [0, 10\,\mathrm s]$.
Figure: $(x, \dot x)$ phase portrait, $t \in [0, 10\,\mathrm s]$.
